        "id": "He8jMyrgtVXz"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Next, let's create a function in Python that implements the \"sigmoid\" function in math, a function that we'll see again later in this course.\n",
        "\n",
        "<center>\n",
        "  $\\displaystyle sigmoid(x) = \\frac{1}{1+e^{-x}}$\n",
        "</center>\n",
        "\n",
        "We'll import the *math* library to do so, and use the built-in *math.exp* function."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "HzLItUFDmoiy"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import math\n",
        "\n",
        "# Define the sigmoid function\n",
        "def sigmoid(x):\n",
        "    return 1 / (1 + math.exp(-x))"
